    "de": {
      "shared_perspectives": "",
      "controversial_points": "Im Diskurs prallen nationale Sicherheitsbedenken auf humanitäre Verpflichtungen. Rechte Medien fordern strengere Grenzkontrollen, während linke Stimmen die Integration und Asylrecht stärken. Parteien nutzen Migration als Wahlthema, wodurch politische Symbolik die sachliche Debatte verdrängt. Medienberichte über Grenzereignisse in Ceuta verstärken das Bild einer unkontrollierbaren Flut, was Ängste in der Bevölkerung schürt."
    },
    "en": {
      "shared_perspectives": "Across the spectrum German outlets agree that the Ceuta influx is being framed as a test of the EU's external border regime and triggers calls for tighter controls at Germany's own frontiers, reflected in repeated references to Schengen suspensions and proposals to extend border checks. They also converge on the view that, despite the rapid return of most migrants to Morocco, the episode reinforces a perception of a migration surge that remains a security and political challenge for Germany.",
      "controversial_points": "German media split between national sovereignty and EU collective responsibility on migration. Right-leaning outlets stress border security, while left-leaning sources emphasize humanitarian duty. The debate pits economic labor shortages against cultural integration anxieties. Political parties use migration as a symbol to mobilize voters, creating polarised narratives. Legal procedures clash with calls for swift deportations, exposing tension between rule of law and populist pressure."
    }
